ase in intracellular Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>, and the release of MCP-1, RANTES and IL-6 by astrocytes treated with opiates and HIV-1 Tat.</article-title><source>Glia</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15630704</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004093-ElHage3"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>El-Hage</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambati</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruce-Keller</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Knapp</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>CCR2 mediates increases in glial activation caused by exposure to HIV-1 Tat and opiates.</article-title><source>J Neuroimmunol</source><volume>178</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16831471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004093-Conant1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Conant</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Garzino-Demo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nath</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McArthur</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Halliday</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Induction of monocyte chemoattractant protein-1 in HIV-1 Tat-stimulated astrocytes and elevation in AIDS dementia.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>3117</fpage><lpage>3121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9501225</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004093-Eugenin1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eugenin</